          "explanation": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>$\\mu = E(X) = 1(0.2)+1.5(0.3)+2(0.1)+2.5(0.4) = 0.2+0.45+0.2+1.0 = 1.85$. $E(X^2) = 1(0.2)+2.25(0.3)+4(0.1)+6.25(0.4) = 0.2+0.675+0.4+2.5 = 3.775$. So $\\sigma^2 = E(X^2)-\\mu^2 = 3.775 - 1.85^2 = 3.775 - 3.4225 = 0.3525 \\approx 0.35$.</p></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>$\\mu = E(X) = 1(0.2)+1.5(0.3)+2(0.1)+2.5(0.4) = 0.2+0.45+0.2+1.0 = 1.85$. $E(X^2) = 1(0.2)+2.25(0.3)+4(0.1)+6.25(0.4) = 0.2+0.675+0.4+2.5 = 3.775$. Vậy $\\sigma^2 = E(X^2)-\\mu^2 = 3.775 - 1.85^2 = 3.775 - 3.4225 = 0.3525 \\approx 0.35$.</p></div>"
